{"number":1212,"title":"Executor invocation cost: per-job minute rounding makes one-item-per-run expensive","body":"GitHub Actions bills each job&#39;s runtime rounded **up** to the next full minute. The queue&#39;s current shape maximizes the number of billed jobs:

- the scheduler workflow fires hourly with **two** jobs (scheduler-run + drain), and the drain dispatches the executor **unconditionally** — 24 near-empty executor runs a day on a quiet repo;
- the executor performs **one item per run** (DESIGN §15.22) and self-re-dispatches for the remainder, so N items cost N workflow runs, each paying checkout/setup spin-up and rounding up.

A working day of ~6 items costs ~55 workflow runs where a handful would do. The owner&#39;s call (2026-08-22, reversing §15.22&#39;s &#34;one run performs one item&#34;): the executor has to execute multiple tasks per invocation, and the model needs a total-executions accounting so a day&#39;s invocation count is asserted, not guessed.

End state:
- one executor run drains the queue until empty (serially — the occupancy model is unchanged, the run boundary is not);
- the scheduler&#39;s drain job dispatches only when something is pickable;
- the operator hold is re-checked between items, so suspension still parks the train at most one item later;
- the simulator carries an Action-executions accounting, and day-long scenarios (scheduled + ad-hoc mix, and a quiet day) assert the totals.

Sliced as sub-issues: the simulator/DESIGN half first, the vendored engine + workflow wiring behind it.","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/issues/1212","user":{"login":"missingbulb","id":73882448,"profile_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73882448?v=4"},"author_association":"OWNER","assignees":[],"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"created_at":"2026-08-22T09:32:38Z","updated_at":"2026-08-22T09:32:38Z","has_parent":false,"has_children":true,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":2,"completed":2,"percent_completed":100},"closed_by_pull_requests":{"total_count":0,"references":[]}}

